## Highlights
MOFs-derived C@ZnCdS MSDCs with superior PEC performance were synthesized for the first time and used as a photoactive material for PEC biosensors.   
This work opens up a promising approach for synthesis of multi-shell hollow carbon materials.   
The photo-generated $\mathbf{e}^{-1}/\mathrm{h}^{+}$ transfer mechanism of TiO2/C@ZnCdS MSDCs/Au for the PEC biosensor was studied.   
The PEC biosensor exhibited an ultra-low detection limit of 2.28 fg mL-1 for CEA with a wide linear response range from 50 fg mL-1 to $500\mathrm{ng}\mathrm{mL}^{-1}$ .
